  "note": "Two hand-written instruction SIDES that must say the same thing, so that publishing via Cursor matches publishing via Claude. Neither side is generated from the other — this file records a human judgement ('I reviewed both; they agree now'), not a build output. Drift = exactly one side moved. `.dentcast/workflows/*.md` IS on the claude side even though both agents read it: `.cursor/rules/dentcast-publishing.mdc` restates the canon's step chain and builder order as a summary, and that summary goes stale the moment a step is added — silently, because nothing but a human reads it. Checked by scripts/check-workflow-sync.mjs (wired into .githooks/pre-commit) and by the PostToolUse hook in .claude/settings.json; update with: node scripts/check-workflow-sync.mjs --ack",
